A||||1||Scott||ECM question...||||5||
Z||000000||Scott||07-17-2001||04:14 PM||||I recently bought a spare ECM for my '85 GT 4 speed.  This new ECM is for a 4 spd '85 GT also.  I'd like to test the new ECM to be sure it works; can I do this by putting it in the car?  Could it damage anything if it's bad?  <BR>TIA<BR>Scott||||reg||5
Z||000001||terryk||07-17-2001||04:32 PM||||It's unlikely the ECM will be damaged unless you reverse the power wires. The inputs and outputs are pretty well protected.<P>Don't do anything blatantly stupid and you should be fine. Also, the ECM shouldn't damage anything either.<P>The correct ECM should be a 1226869.<P>Since you will be removing the power from the ECM's, be prepared for the engine to idle a bit odd while the ECM learns the new BLM cells. Same for cruise and tip in. It will learn fairly quick. Just go cruising and let it idle for a few minutes at the end. It will hit most of the cells.<P>Terry<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 07-17-2001).]||||reg||14
